# Planner consumer #1 — bare-param mutation inside an `if` branch (the scope
# pre-header materialize class). `lower_if` wraps each branch in save_locals/
# restore_locals; the in-body CoW materialize rebind was reverted and the read
# after the `if` resolved the stale pre-branch borrow (printed 4,4). The
# pre-scope hoist (dispatch-arm `materialize_scope_carried_bare_params`) clones
# once BEFORE the branch dispatch so the fresh owned local dominates the merge —
# the private-copy pop now persists (3), the caller is untouched (4).
# ggdef-adjudicated 3,4 (in-subset: bare Vector param, if, mutating method, print).
void f(Vector[int] xs):
    if xs.len() > 2:
        xs.pop()
    print(xs.len())

void main():
    Vector[int] a = [1, 2, 3, 4]
    f(a)
    print(a.len())
